      "impact_statement": "CVE-2024-7254: parsing untrusted Protocol Buffers data that contains an unbounded number of nested groups or SGROUP tags, as unknown fields with DiscardUnknownFieldsParser or the Java Protobuf Lite parser, or against map fields, recurses without limit and overflows the stack (https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/security/advisories/GHSA-735f-pc8j-v9w8). The advisory covers the Java runtime libraries (Maven com.google.protobuf:protobuf-java, protobuf-javalite, protobuf-kotlin and protobuf-kotlin-lite) and the Ruby google-protobuf gem, fixed in 3.25.5, 4.27.5 and 4.28.2; it does not list the C++ library, the compiler or the Python library. Debian ships the Java runtime as libprotobuf-java, an architecture-independent package, and its fix for trixie in protobuf 3.21.12-11+deb13u1 (\"Complete fix of CVE-2024-7254 (closes: #1082381): add recursion checks and recursion limit, add tests\", https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-7254) changes only the Java sources and test protos. The DHI protobuf packages for Debian 13 are rebuilds of Debian's trixie protobuf that build only the architecture-specific packages and leave out the Ruby binding, so libprotobuf-java and ruby-google-protobuf are not part of this owner. Unpacked every protobuf package now published in the DHI Debian repository (3.21.12-11+deb13u1: libprotobuf32t64, libprotobuf-lite32t64, libprotoc32t64, protobuf-compiler and python3-protobuf with their -dbgsym packages, plus libprotobuf-dev and libprotoc-dev, for amd64 and arm64): none contains a .jar, a .class file, a Kotlin file or Ruby code. The only Java-related files are two example programs, AddPerson.java and ListPeople.java, under /usr/share/doc/protobuf-compiler/examples, and the C++ headers for protoc's Java, Kotlin and Ruby code generators in libprotoc-dev; the Java runtime parser the fix changes is not shipped."
    },
